title":"Senior SQL Server Database Administrator","company":"GSSTech Group","location":"Bangalore","date_posted":"2026-09-07","url":"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=e20d63816971fba7&from=serp&vjs=3","experience":"Senior","skills":[1,12,14,15,19,34,102,103,110,111],"is_walkin":false,"indeed_jk":"e20d63816971fba7","permanent_url":"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=e20d63816971fba7&from=serp&vjs=3"},{"title":"Database Administrator","company":"Nextwebi IT solutions","location":"Bangalore","date_posted":"2026-09-08","url":"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=0dc6214db9e35535&from=serp&vjs=3","experience":"1-3 Yrs","skills":[1,7,12,13,14,17,33,34],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Job Profile: Database Administrator job at High\\-Scale Food\\-Tech Unicorn**\n\n**Location:** Bangalore \\| Karnataka\n\n**Years of Experience:** 1 to 3 Years\n\n**ABOUT THE TEAM \\& ROLE:**\n\nThe production engineering team is responsible for the smooth operation and security of the production infrastructure. We strive to excel and continuously improve on key operational pillars (Reliability, Security, Observability, Elasticity, and Governance). We design, build, and operate Product tech cloud infrastructure and supporting platforms to provide a flawless customer experience.\n\nThis role will contribute to:\n\n\u25cf Reliability, availability, and security of the critical database infrastructure at AWS (MySQL, DynamoDB, Elasticsearch, and Redis).\n\n\u25cf Observing, identifying, and correcting performance and scale bottlenecks of these databases.\n\n\u25cf Automating and codifying repetitive operations and providing self\\-service tools.\n\n\u25cf De\\-risking data availability using highly consistent data backup and restore methods.\n\n**What qualities are we looking for?**\n\n\u25cf Familiarity with software engineering practices including unit testing, code reviews, and design documentation.\n\n\u25cf An interest in building internal products with other engineers as your customers.\n\n\u25cf Track record of building self\\-service and high\\-quality platforms for developers with a customer\\-driven mindset.\n\n\u25cf Curiosity about how things work and a love for sharing that knowledge with others.\n\n\u25cf 1\u20133 years of professional experience in a software environment.\n\n\u25cf B.Tech/M.Tech in Computer Science or equivalent from a reputed college.\n\n**What you should have?**\n\n\u25cf Hands\\-on experience with datastores like MySQL and PostgreSQL on AWS or similar infrastructure platforms.\n\n\u25cf Hands\\-on experience driving major version upgrades on MySQL is preferred.\n\n\u25cf Hands\\-on experience with datastore management principles and practices (availability, backup management, performance management, security, proactive monitoring, encryption, etc.).\n\n\u25cf Experience in building and operating large distributed datastore infrastructure.\n\n\u25cf Understanding of operating systems, virtualization, and containerization.\n\n\u25cf Hands\\-on coding experience in languages like Bash, Python, or Go.\n\n\u25cf Strong debugging and problem\\-solving skills.\n\n*We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law.*\n\nPay: \u20b91,000,000\\.00 \\- \u20b91,200,000\\.00 per year\n\nBenefits:\n\n* Health insurance\n* Provident Fund\n\nWork Location: In person","indeed_jk":"0dc6214db9e35535","permanent_url":"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=0dc6214db9e35535&from=serp&vjs=3"},{"title":"Sr Database Administrator","company":"Disney Experiences","location":"Bangalore","date_posted":"2026-09-08","url":"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=ef7a756287940184&from=serp&vjs=3","experience":"5 Yrs","skills":[1,2,7,12,13,14,19,20,34,102,103,104],"is_walkin":false,"description":"The Sr Database Administrator for Disney Experiences plays a key role in ensuring reliable, secure, and highly available database platforms that power magical guest and cast experiences across parks, resorts, cruise, vacation, travel, retail, and consumer operations. In this P3 professional role, you will operate as a skilled, independent worker and effective mentor, solving complex problems and offering new perspectives on existing solutions.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n\n\nIn this role, you will take ownership of end\\-to\\-end database infrastructure across on\\-premises and cloud environments that support Disney's creative, customer\\-focused, and service\\-minded experiences worldwide. You will act as a proficient problem\\-solver and resource for colleagues with less experience, working independently with minimal guidance while occasionally leading small, low\\-risk initiatives that enhance system performance, resiliency, and availability. This role matters because robust database platforms are essential to delivering seamless, innovative guest and cast experiences, and success requires a skilled, detail\\-oriented, team\\-oriented administrator with strong communication and mentoring capabilities.\n\n* Build, deploy, and ensure 24/7/365 availability of database infrastructure supporting Disney Experiences technology solutions.\n* Provide operational support and administration for relational and NoSQL databases across on\\-premises and cloud environments, including Amazon RDS or similar database\\-as\\-a\\-service platforms.\n* Analyze, design, and deploy fault\\-tolerant, distributed, and highly available database architectures for high\\-volume, high\\-availability systems.\n* Perform database performance tuning, troubleshooting, and administration, including proactive identification of issues and design of creative remediation solutions.\n* Plan and implement infrastructure changes through capacity forecasting, resource utilization analysis, software release cycles, and right\\-sizing activities.\n* Implement and manage database availability monitoring, metrics, 